WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.678
Chaplin: Good day, young lady.

2
00:00:01.679 --> 00:00:03.656
It’s nice to meet you.

3
00:00:03.657 --> 00:00:05.214
Girl: Who are

4
00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:09.227
you? Chaplin: Who am I? My name is Charlie

5
00:00:09.228 --> 00:00:13.693
Chaplin. I was the most famous silent movie actor in the

6
00:00:13.694 --> 00:00:18.770
world. Girl: What are silent

7
00:00:18.771 --> 00:00:21.996
movies? Chaplin: Silent movies were the first kind of

8
00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:25.829
movie. In silent movies, the actors do not

9
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.220
talk. Girl: No talking? That sounds

10
00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:34.149
boring. Chaplin: Absolutely not! Silent movies are exciting

11
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.625
and funny. Millions of people saw my

12
00:00:36.626 --> 00:00:38.634
movies. Everyone loved

13
00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:40.628
them. Girl:

14
00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:43.237
Really? Chaplin: Do you like to read

15
00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:46.910
storybooks? Well, silent movies are like

16
00:00:46.911 --> 00:00:51.312
storybooks. But they are much better because the pictures move.

17
00:00:51.313 --> 00:00:56.738
That’s why they are called movies—because they have moving pictures.

18
00:00:56.739 --> 00:01:02.862
Girl: Movies have moving pictures. Ha-ha!

19
00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:06.243
Why did you stop making silent movies?

20
00:01:06.244 --> 00:01:12.580
Chaplin: These days, people don’t want to see silent movies; everyone wants talkies.

21
00:01:12.581 --> 00:01:14.342
Girl: Talkies?

22
00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:18.210
Chaplin: That’s the word people first used for talking

23
00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:22.585
movies. Movies where the actors talked were called talkies.

24
00:01:22.586 --> 00:01:25.252
Girl: Did you come from Hollywood?

25
00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:28.992
Chaplin: No, I was born far away from

26
00:01:28.993 --> 00:01:31.173
Hollywood. I came from

27
00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:36.608
England. I was born on April 16, 1889, in

28
00:01:36.609 --> 00:01:43.737
London. Like me, my father and mother were both entertainers.

29
00:01:43.738 --> 00:01:46.375
Girl: Were they rich and famous?

30
00:01:46.376 --> 00:01:49.025
Chaplin: No, we were very

31
00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:52.348
poor. But my parents gave me something better than money.

32
00:01:52.349 --> 00:01:59.014
They gave me the talent to entertain people.

33
00:01:59.015 --> 00:02:03.750
When I was very young, they taught me how to sing and dance. When

34
00:02:03.751 --> 00:02:09.095
I was five years old, I sang and danced in front of many people. Girl:

35
00:02:09.096 --> 00:02:10.768
Did they like you? Chaplin:

36
00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:12.577
Of course, they did.

37
00:02:12.578 --> 00:02:16.793
They loved me and they threw money at me.

38
00:02:16.794 --> 00:02:19.145
Girl: That must have been exciting.

39
00:02:19.146 --> 00:02:24.520
Chaplin: It was. My mother said I would be the most famous person in the

40
00:02:24.521 --> 00:02:29.734
world. But then, sadly, my father died when I was twelve years

41
00:02:29.735 --> 00:02:36.610
old. When he died, my mother became very sick as well.

42
00:02:36.611 --> 00:02:40.830
After that, my brother and I had to go to the workhouse.

43
00:02:40.831 --> 00:02:42.919
Girl: What is a workhouse?

44
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:48.873
Chaplin: It was a terrible place where poor children had to go when their families had no

45
00:02:48.874 --> 00:02:54.305
money. The children had to work very hard from morning until

46
00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:57.381
night. Girl: How did you become a famous movie

47
00:02:57.382 --> 00:03:00.458
star? Chaplin: First, I became a stage

48
00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:04.214
actor. Then, I joined the Casey Circus as a

49
00:03:04.215 --> 00:03:08.673
mime. Girl: Mime? What’s

50
00:03:08.674 --> 00:03:13.887
that? Chaplin: A mime is an actor who uses only his body and

51
00:03:13.888 --> 00:03:16.105
his face. Watch! I’ll show

52
00:03:16.106 --> 00:03:18.934
you! Girl: Ha-ha! You’re

53
00:03:18.935 --> 00:03:21.129
funny. Chaplin: That’s what everyone

54
00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.289
said. They said I was a very

55
00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.899
funny mime. So I decided to become a silent

56
00:03:27.902 --> 00:03:31.161
comedian. I made everyone

57
00:03:31.162 --> 00:03:36.532
laugh. Soon, I went to the United States and started making

58
00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:41.863
movies. In 1914, I acted in my first full-length silent

59
00:03:41.864 --> 00:03:44.854
movie. It was called Making a Living

60
00:03:44.855 --> 00:03:49.681
. Then I created my most famous character, the Tramp.

61
00:03:49.682 --> 00:03:57.264
With my funny little suit, mustache, and cane, I made the whole world laugh.

62
00:03:57.265 --> 00:03:59.941
Girl: I guess everyone loved you.

63
00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:02.585
Chaplin: No, not everyone liked

64
00:04:02.586 --> 00:04:07.281
me. In the United States, some policemen thought that I was a troublemaker.

65
00:04:07.282 --> 00:04:15.211
Some of my movies made them angry, so I had to go back to England.

66
00:04:15.212 --> 00:04:18.202
Girl: Did you ever go back to America?

67
00:04:18.203 --> 00:04:20.915
Chaplin: Yes, I went one more

68
00:04:20.916 --> 00:04:26.559
time. In 1972, I was given a great honor at the Academy Awards.

69
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:32.251
That was one of the happiest moments of my life.

